<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-10-01T19:37:05+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Thu, 01 Oct 2026 19:37:05 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Reggie Leaks Cenat DMs: streamer says ‘cry for help’ was ignored; Fanum urges mental reset]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134605430.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Reggie, also known as Lil Rodney Son, shared screenshots of messages he sent to Kai Cenat after saying he needed to speak with him privately. He also posted a long message from Fanum, who encouraged him to step away from online pressure and keep going. The posts came after Reggie’s recent videos about his personal struggles and Clover Boys fallout.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/reggie-leaks-kai-cenat-conversation-claims-streamer-left-his-cry-for-help-message-unanswered/articleshow/134605430.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/reggie-leaks-kai-cenat-conversation-claims-streamer-left-his-cry-for-help-message-unanswered/articleshow/134605430.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T04:31:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sumit Roy</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134605433,imgsize-741691.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Reggie Leaks Cenat DMs: Streamer posts ‘cry for help’ messages; Fanum urges focus on mental health]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134605414.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Reggie, also known as Lil Rodney Son, has shared private DMs with Kai Cenat after claiming he urgently needed his support. The messages show Reggie asking Cenat to answer his call and describing it as a “cry for help.” Reggie also shared a lengthy message from Fanum, who urged him to step away from online pressure and focus on his well-being. Agent 00 declined to discuss the controversy.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/kai-cenat-faces-fresh-backlash-as-reggie-leaks-private-dms-after-desperate-plea/articleshow/134605414.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/kai-cenat-faces-fresh-backlash-as-reggie-leaks-private-dms-after-desperate-plea/articleshow/134605414.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T05:52:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134605444,imgsize-164100.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Thomas Stone paid £400 for a 442-acre Maryland property in 1770; after 166 years in his family...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134619497.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Originally founded by John Barefoot and expanded by Daniel Jenifer, Haberdeventure estate is steeped in history. Thomas Stone bought the estate in 1770, preserving it within his family for 166 years. A significant fire in 1977 led to protective actions and, in 1978, it became the Thomas Stone National Historic Site. Following restorations completed in 1997, it now spans 328 acres, serving as a historical hub for inquisitive visitors.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/thomas-stone-paid-400-for-a-442-acre-maryland-property-in-1770-after-166-years-in-his-family-and-a-devastating-house-fire-the-estate-became-a-national-historic-site-honouring-the-declaration-signer/articleshow/134619497.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/thomas-stone-paid-400-for-a-442-acre-maryland-property-in-1770-after-166-years-in-his-family-and-a-devastating-house-fire-the-estate-became-a-national-historic-site-honouring-the-declaration-signer/articleshow/134619497.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T19:03:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134620814,imgsize-2174183.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Nepal avalanche kills 15 workers at Himlung Himal camp, one still missing]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134620619.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[An avalanche struck the base camp of Himlung Himal, resulting in the deaths of at least 15 Nepali workers. The workers were preparing for an all-women climbing group that was scheduled to arrive soon. Rescuers recovered the bodies, but one worker remains missing after poor weather hampered operations. The incident has been reported as the deadliest of the autumn climbing season in Nepal.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/south-asia/nepal-avalanche-kills-15-workers-at-himlung-himal-camp-one-still-missing/articleshow/134620619.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/south-asia/nepal-avalanche-kills-15-workers-at-himlung-himal-camp-one-still-missing/articleshow/134620619.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T19:00:45+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134620684,imgsize-87654.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1930s, family bought Montana ranch; 884 acres now protected from development]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134616473.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-the-1930s-bob-andersons-grandfather-bought-a-montana-ranch-nearly-a-century-later-the-family-permanently-protected-all-884-acres-from-subdivision-to-keep-it-in-agriculture/articleshow/134616473.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-the-1930s-bob-andersons-grandfather-bought-a-montana-ranch-nearly-a-century-later-the-family-permanently-protected-all-884-acres-from-subdivision-to-keep-it-in-agriculture/articleshow/134616473.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T19:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134616600,imgsize-633884.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[North Carolina Family bought 600 acres in 1811; 214 years later, 298 acres protected from development]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134619746.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a remarkable effort to maintain their agricultural heritage, a North Carolina family has successfully preserved 298 acres of land from development over seven generations. Acquired in 1811 by John W. Caldwell and Nancy Hartfield, this property operates as a working forest. The enacted conservation easement guarantees that this land will remain untouched by housing or commercial ventures, earning recognition from conservation groups for their sustainable management practices.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-north-carolina-family-bought-600-acres-in-1811-and-kept-part-of-the-land-for-seven-generations-214-years-later-a-conservation-deal-protected-298-acres-from-becoming-housing-or-commercial-developments/articleshow/134619746.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-north-carolina-family-bought-600-acres-in-1811-and-kept-part-of-the-land-for-seven-generations-214-years-later-a-conservation-deal-protected-298-acres-from-becoming-housing-or-commercial-developments/articleshow/134619746.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T18:29:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134619910,imgsize-1619249.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2020, Roger Daltrey and his family started Lakedown Brewing; three years later, the business...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134619111.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Founded in 2020 by Roger Daltrey and his family, Lakedown Brewing Co. is a charming microbrewery based in East Sussex. Dedicated to crafting easy-drinking beers from high-quality ingredients, they also oversee the Lakedown Trout Fishery, creating a picturesque setting for visitors. Committed to the local community, the brewery actively supports youth music training initiatives, with their beers available in many independent pubs around Sussex.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-2020-roger-daltrey-and-his-family-started-lakedown-brewing-three-years-later-the-business-opened-its-own-brewery-on-his-600-acre-sussex-farm-where-he-had-created-trout-lakes-decades-earlier/articleshow/134619111.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-2020-roger-daltrey-and-his-family-started-lakedown-brewing-three-years-later-the-business-opened-its-own-brewery-on-his-600-acre-sussex-farm-where-he-had-created-trout-lakes-decades-earlier/articleshow/134619111.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T18:05:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134619428,imgsize-806429.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Anonymous donor gave Ali's favourite Louisville park $5m: ‘lover of parks’]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134619506.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/anonymous-donor-gave-muhammad-alis-favourite-louisville-park-5-million-for-restoration-then-only-said-they-were-a-lover-of-parks/articleshow/134619506.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/anonymous-donor-gave-muhammad-alis-favourite-louisville-park-5-million-for-restoration-then-only-said-they-were-a-lover-of-parks/articleshow/134619506.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T18:28:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134619820,imgsize-2091023.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New US visa rule from October 1: Expanded social media screening for I, TN and TD visa applicant