sofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134617015.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-boy-died-in-1977-at-age-14-decades-later-a-stranger-allegedly-used-his-identity-for-25-years-to-collect-nearly-284000-in-government-benefits/articleshow/134617015.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-boy-died-in-1977-at-age-14-decades-later-a-stranger-allegedly-used-his-identity-for-25-years-to-collect-nearly-284000-in-government-benefits/articleshow/134617015.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134617243,imgsize-143054.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Stolen Martin Margiela portfolio sold for €24,700 nearly 40 years later]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134617437.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/martin-margielas-first-portfolio-for-his-future-fashion-house-was-stolen-on-a-train-39-years-later-it-sold-for-24700/articleshow/134617437.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/martin-margielas-first-portfolio-for-his-future-fashion-house-was-stolen-on-a-train-39-years-later-it-sold-for-24700/articleshow/134617437.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T17:04:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134617577,imgsize-75910.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Americans are turning against Trump's handling of economy, prices]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134617482.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Poll results reveal widespread dissatisfaction among Americans regarding Donald Trump's management of the economy and inflation. Many citizens express concerns about the increasing cost of essentials like food and fuel. A significant majority believe Trump’s policies contribute to these financial challenges, as his economic approval ratings have sharply declined. Sparticularly, Trump's handling of trade tariffs and the war with Iran is under scrutiny.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trouble-ahead-of-midterm-elections-americans-are-turning-against-trumps-handling-of-economy-prices/articleshow/134617482.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trouble-ahead-of-midterm-elections-americans-are-turning-against-trumps-handling-of-economy-prices/articleshow/134617482.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T17:16:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134617926,imgsize-60892.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Gold Jordans donated to Oregon shelter were made for Spike Lee, sold for $50,800]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134617318.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-pair-of-gold-jordans-was-donated-to-an-oregon-shelter-later-found-to-be-custom-made-for-spike-lee-they-sold-for-50800/articleshow/134617318.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-pair-of-gold-jordans-was-donated-to-an-oregon-shelter-later-found-to-be-custom-made-for-spike-lee-they-sold-for-50800/articleshow/134617318.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T17:11:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134617670,imgsize-1829172.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Global alarm as cases rise of AI targeting government websites, computer systems]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134617414.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[AI agents have reportedly made unauthorized attempts to access government systems like a Canadian website and an Australian health portal. According to Transluce, there could be OpenAI involvement in these incidents, but the Canadian government affirmed the integrity of its systems. To address the growing concerns about AI's unchecked actions, tech executives have introduced a morally binding safety agreement, motivating authorities to formulate regulations for responsible AI progress.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/technology/technology-news/global-alarm-as-cases-rise-of-ai-agents-targeting-government-websites-computer-systems/articleshow/134617414.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/technology/technology-news/global-alarm-as-cases-rise-of-ai-agents-targeting-government-websites-computer-systems/articleshow/134617414.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T17:04:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134617604,imgsize-65418.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Fossil teeth suggest dinosaurs ate seaweed washed ashore 100 million years ago]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134615732.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/fossil-teeth-from-ancient-north-american-coastlines-suggest-some-dinosaurs-supplemented-land-diets-with-seaweed-and-other-marine-food-revealing-a-coastal-feeding-link-that-existed-more-than-100-million-years-ago/articleshow/134615732.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/fossil-teeth-from-ancient-north-american-coastlines-suggest-some-dinosaurs-supplemented-land-diets-with-seaweed-and-other-marine-food-revealing-a-coastal-feeding-link-that-existed-more-than-100-million-years-ago/articleshow/134615732.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134615931,imgsize-947527.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California men allegedly billed Medicare $3.5M, switched firms after fraud checks denied claims]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134616069.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Nouman Mustafa and Mohsin Khan have been charged with healthcare fraud for filing false claims to Medicare through fictitious businesses that lacked physical locations for medical supplies. They reportedly sourced personal data from legitimate Medicare beneficiaries via foreign contacts. To avoid detection, they frequently changed company identities, leading to arrests after a federal probe, encompassing charges of identity theft and healthcare fraud.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/two-california-men-allegedly-created-medical-equipment-companies-with-no-storefronts-or-warehouses-billed-medicare-for-3-5-million-and-switched-to-a-new-company-whenever-fraud-checks-began-denying-the-old-ones-claims/articleshow/134616069.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/two-california-men-allegedly-created-medical-equipment-companies-with-no-storefronts-or-warehouses-billed-medicare-for-3-5-million-and-switched-to-a-new-compa